    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.91) and **Luis Arraez** (67.31) anchor our lineup, benefiting significantly from matchups against pitchers with xERAs near or above 4.50. **Geraldo Perdomo** stands out as the primary play; the combination of a favorable 4.94 xERA from his opponent and a spot in the two-hole provides the optimal environment for him to generate counting stats. Meanwhile, **Jung Hoo Lee** (63.73) and **Tyler Freeman** (63.09) are critical assets today. **Jung Hoo Lee** is positioned to capitalize on Gusto\u2019s slow delivery, which boosts his steal probability, while **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a high-yield park factor of +14%, effectively masking the marginal difficulty of facing a sub-4.00 xERA arm.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Jonathan Aranda** (41.72), who fell just outside our efficiency threshold. While **Jonathan Aranda** offers a solid xwOBA of .375, his negative platoon split against a left-handed starter and a low floor forced him to the bench in favor of more efficient, right-handed-heavy options like **Matt Chapman** (61.19), who continues to thrive in favorable platoon spots. Elsewhere, **Bryson Stott** (42.65) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (41.89) are being deployed with extreme caution. **Bryson Stott** is hampered by an elite-level opposing catcher and a bottom-of-the-order assignment, while **Jeremiah Jackson** faces a stiff challenge against a 3.34 xERA starter, making both players high-risk options despite their inclusion.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the volatile nature of these matchups; **Taylor Ward** (46.18) and **Gavin Sheets** (46.12) are currently in the marginal tier and could easily slip below our desired floor if early at-bats against their respective elite-arm opponents go poorly. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains sidelined, we are continuing to monitor bench depth like **Lawrence Butler**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Will Smith**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Ryan Waldschmidt** for any late-breaking lineup changes that might necessitate a shift in our strategy before the first pitch.",
